{"translation":{"id":"fra_jnd","name":"Bible J.N. Darby","website":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=frajnd","licenseUrl":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=frajnd","licenseNotes":null,"shortName":"JND","englishName":"French: Bible J.N. Darby","language":"fra","textDirection":"ltr","sha256":"121a3f4841e42965f22ebebcf5a8578a12578ec30eaf1ca7ae4e46d5d85ccb80","availableFormats":["json"],"listOfBooksApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/books.json","numberOfBooks":66,"totalNumberOfChapters":1189,"totalNumberOfVerses":31170,"languageName":"français","languageEnglishName":"French"},"book":{"id":"PSA","translationId":"fra_jnd","name":"Les Psaumes","commonName":"Les Psaumes","title":"Les Psaumes","order":19,"numberOfChapters":150,"sha256":"4c48a766d24644f7ef347ae1395ef8ddb5d363cc30acf1733162d22f071b120e","firstChapterNumber":1,"firstChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/1.json","lastChapterNumber":150,"lastChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/150.json","totalNumberOfVerses":2527},"chapter":{"number":58,"content":[{"type":"verse","number":1,"content":[{"text":"Au chef de musique. Al-Tashkheth","poem":1},{"noteId":155},{"text":". De David. Mictam","poem":1},{"noteId":156},{"text":".","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":2,"content":[{"text":"Est-ce que vraiment la justice se tait ? Prononcez-vous [ce qui est juste] ? Vous, fils des hommes, jugez-vous avec droiture ?","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":3,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Bien plutôt, dans le cœur, vous commettez des iniquités ; dans le pays, vous pesez","poem":1},{"noteId":157},{"text":"la violence de vos mains.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":4,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Les méchants se sont égarés dès la matrice ; ils errent dès le ventre, parlant le mensonge.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Ils ont un venin semblable au venin d’un serpent, comme l’aspic sourd qui se bouche l’oreille,","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Qui n’entend pas la voix des charmeurs, du sorcier expert en sorcelleries.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Ô Dieu ! dans leur bouche brise leurs dents ; Éternel ! arrache les grosses dents des jeunes lions.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Qu’ils se fondent comme des eaux qui s’écoulent ! S’il ajuste ses flèches, qu’elles soient comme cassées","poem":1},{"noteId":158},{"text":"!","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":9,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Qu’ils soient comme une limace qui va se fondant ! Comme l’avorton d’une femme, qu’ils ne voient pas le soleil !","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":10,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Avant que vos chaudières aient senti les épines, vertes ou enflammées, le tourbillon les emportera.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":11,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Le juste se réjouira quand il verra la vengeance ; il lavera ses pieds","poem":1},{"noteId":159},{"text":"dans le sang du méchant.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":12,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Et l’homme dira : Certainement il y a un fruit pour le juste, certainement il y a un Dieu qui juge sur la terre.","poem":1}]}],"footnotes":[{"noteId":155,"caller":"a","text":"ne détruis pas.","reference":{"chapter":58,"verse":1}},{"noteId":156,"caller":"b","text":"mot d’un sens incertain.","reference":{"chapter":58,"verse":1}},{"noteId":157,"caller":"c","text":"ou : réfléchissez à.","reference":{"chapter":58,"verse":3}},{"noteId":158,"caller":"d","text":"c.-à-d. : la pointe cassée.","reference":{"chapter":58,"verse":8}},{"noteId":159,"caller":"e","text":"litt. : ses pas.","reference":{"chapter":58,"verse":11}}]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/58.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/59.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/57.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":12}